# Project Details

## Overview

The Real-Time Testing API project enables developers and QA teams to:

* Test APIs automatically
* Monitor endpoint performance in real time
* Validate request and response structures
* Generate execution reports
* Track API uptime and latency
* Simulate concurrent API requests

The system helps identify failures quickly and improves debugging efficiency by providing real-time logs and analytics.

---

# Key Features

## Real-Time API Monitoring

* Continuously tracks API response status
* Displays live response time metrics
* Detects downtime and failures instantly

## Automated API Testing

* Executes predefined API test cases automatically
* Supports GET, POST, PUT, DELETE requests
* Validates headers, payloads, and status codes

## Performance Analytics

* Measures:

  * Response time
  * Throughput
  * Success/failure rates
  * API latency

## Live Dashboard

* Displays:

  * API health status
  * Real-time logs
  * Test execution reports
  * Request history

## Concurrent Request Simulation

* Simulates multiple users hitting APIs simultaneously
* Useful for stress and load testing

## Authentication & Security

* JWT-based authentication
* Secure API access
* Protected testing routes

---

# Architecture Flow

1. User submits API endpoint for testing
2. Backend processes the request
3. Automated test engine executes API calls
4. Results are validated
5. Real-time updates are pushed using WebSockets
6. Dashboard displays analytics instantly
7. Logs and reports are stored in the database

